# No Co-authored-by: Cursor

**Hard rule.** Never leave a Cursor or agent co-author trailer on a commit.

- Forbidden in the final commit message: `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Co-authored-by: cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any similar Cursor/agent trailer.
- Do not write these lines yourself. If the environment injects them after `git commit`, that still counts as a failure — rewrite before you stop.
- After every commit: `git log -1 --format='%B'`. If a forbidden trailer appears, rewrite:

```bash
NEW=$(git commit-tree "$(git rev-parse 'HEAD^{tree}')" -p "$(git rev-parse 'HEAD^')" -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
<same subject and body, no Co-authored-by>
EOF
)")
git reset --soft "$NEW"
git log -1 --format='%B'   # must show no Co-authored-by
```

- Repo policy: `AGENTS.md` (Commits) and `CONTRIBUTING.md` (Commit conventions).
